    {
      "id": "fb-001",
      "question": "What happens when a SIM goes offline?",
      "shape": "document",
      "guard": "fix",
      "blocked_on": null,
      "asked_as": "1a1db65e-52d5-493b-a1a9-7e495005530a",
      "http_status": 200,
      "seconds": 29.56,
      "answer": "When a SIM goes offline, it can lead to several challenges in fleet management and operations. The system is designed to help manage SIM cards effectively to avoid such issues:\n\n1. **Linkage**: Each SIM should be visibly linked to a specific tracker, asset, branch, and department to avoid confusion during support calls and speed up troubleshooting.\n\n2. **Data-Spend Summaries**: Finance managers can access daily, weekly, and monthly data-spend summaries by telco, country, product, and customer account to monitor connectivity expenses and prevent unnoticed margin erosion.\n\n3. **Automatic Data Ingestion**: The system aims to ingest SIM data automatically from telco APIs to avoid manual updates and stale records, improving accuracy and operating efficiency.\n\n4. **SIM Commissioning**: Guided steps for SIM commissioning capture essential details like ICCID, IMEI, APN, test signal, and first heartbeat to ensure correct installation and reduce avoidable repeat visits.\n\n5. **Roaming Status**: Cross-border fleet owners can view roaming status by country and estimated cost impact to make early decisions and avoid shock bills on regional routes.\n\n6. **Bundle Recommendations**: The system recommends suitable roaming or local bundles for the corridor an asset is entering to keep units online at lower costs.\n\n7. **Bundle Monitoring**: Support engineers can monitor bundle remaining percentages and projected depletion dates to intervene before a unit goes offline, reducing downtime.\n\n8. **Network Monitoring**: For personnel monitoring, wearable and smartphone SIMs show network type, signal strength, and recent connectivity gaps to determine if staff are truly unreachable or merely inactive.\n\nThese features are designed to prevent and manage the impact of a SIM going offline, though I can't confirm which parts are live for your account.\n\nSource: OLIWA User Stories — this is the documented design; I can't confirm from here which parts are live.",
      "tools_used": [
        "waswa_context",
        "unit_find(all, prefetched)",
        "knowledge_search(SIM goes offline)"
      ],
